{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.GermCommutatorQCurvature","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.GermCommutatorQCurvature","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LocalQ.ObservationParallelogram.curvature_antisymm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LocalQ.ObservationParallelogram.curvature_antisymm","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/germ-commutator-q-curvature.lean#L98-L105","doc":"**Antisymmetry of the q-curvature.** Swapping the two observers\nnegates the curvature: `F_q` is a genuine 2-form on the loop. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LocalQ.ObservationParallelogram.agree_iff_flat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LocalQ.ObservationParallelogram.agree_iff_flat","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/germ-commutator-q-curvature.lean#L92-L96","doc":"The two observers **agree** (vanishing parallelogram) iff the\n`q`-curvature vanishes — the boson / `q`-flat case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LocalQ.ObservationParallelogram.commutator_eq_curvature","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LocalQ.ObservationParallelogram.commutator_eq_curvature","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/germ-commutator-q-curvature.lean#L82-L90","doc":"**Germ-commutator = q-curvature.** The commutator of the two\nobservations equals the `q`-curvature 2-form on the loop: the\nlinear (`1·δq`) terms of the two path-ordered transports cancel and\nonly the second-order ordering defect `δq₁δq₂ − δq₂δq₁` survives.\nDerived by non-commutative ring algebra, not assumed. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:germ-commutator-q-curvature","label":"prop:germ-commutator-q-curvature","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/germ-commutator-q-curvature.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LocalQ.ObservationParallelogram.Fq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LocalQ.ObservationParallelogram.Fq","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/germ-commutator-q-curvature.lean#L74-L80","doc":"The `q`-curvature 2-form evaluated on the loop, **defined** as the\ntransport defect around the parallelogram: the difference between\ntransporting first along observer 1 then observer 2 and the\nopposite ordering,\n`F_q = (1 + δq₁)(1 + δq₂) − (1 + δq₂)(1 + δq₁)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LocalQ.ObservationParallelogram.transport₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LocalQ.ObservationParallelogram.transport₂","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/germ-commutator-q-curvature.lean#L71-L72","doc":"First-order transport of the second observation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LocalQ.ObservationParallelogram.transport₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LocalQ.ObservationParallelogram.transport₁","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/germ-commutator-q-curvature.lean#L66-L69","doc":"First-order transport of the first observation: the germ-level\nincrement acts on the fibre as `1 + δq₁` (identity plus the\nperturbation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LocalQ.ObservationParallelogram.δq₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LocalQ.ObservationParallelogram.δq₂","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/germ-commutator-q-curvature.lean#L62-L62","doc":"Second observer's germ-level perturbation of the substrate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LocalQ.ObservationParallelogram.δq₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LocalQ.ObservationParallelogram.δq₁","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/germ-commutator-q-curvature.lean#L60-L60","doc":"First observer's germ-level perturbation of the substrate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LocalQ.ObservationParallelogram.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LocalQ.ObservationParallelogram.mk","kind":"ctor","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/germ-commutator-q-curvature.lean#L58-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LocalQ.ObservationParallelogram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LocalQ.ObservationParallelogram","kind":"structure","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/germ-commutator-q-curvature.lean#L52-L62","doc":"**Two-observer parallelogram** at a point `p`: the pair of\nobservation perturbations `δq₁, δq₂ ∈ R` spanning the infinitesimal\nloop.  Only the two increments are data; the `q`-curvature on the\nloop is *defined* below as the transport defect around the\nparallelogram, and the parallelogram identity `[δq₁, δq₂] = F_q`\nis *derived* (`commutator_eq_curvature`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LocalQ.obsCommutator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LocalQ.obsCommutator","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/germ-commutator-q-curvature.lean#L47-L50","doc":"The observation commutator (ring/Lie bracket) of two germ-level\nsubstrate perturbations at a point `p`. Non-trivial precisely\nbecause the germ algebra `A/𝔪_p²` is non-commutative. ","signatureChunk":0}]}